# ═══ META-LESSONS ═══
L1: Cross-crate struct field addition (HookRuntime.contract_attestation) caught at compile time by 1 site (Self construction) — fast feedback
L2: Drift corrector pure fn design (no IO) made it trivial to add a new axis without state management
L3: Pre-existing test contract (handle_pre_compact returns String::new()) is a foot-gun for future changes — R1 of plan was correctly predicted
L4: Honest carve-out (model-layer attention non-eviction) is the value-add of documenting, not the value-add of working around
L5: For P3.2 (session_start), the function takes &mut HookRuntime so we can update state; for P3.3 (instructions_loaded) the function takes &HookRuntime, so we can only log a re-pin — different signatures dictate different behaviors

